<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Paris (1857)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1857">1857</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-persian-war">Anglo-Persian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1856">Treaty of Paris</a> of 4 March 1857 ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-persian-war">Anglo-Persian War</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, which had begun after Iranian forces took the Afghan city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herat">Herat</a> in 1856. Iran agreed to withdraw from Herat and to renounce all claims to Afghan territory, while Britain evacuated the ports and islands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a> that it had occupied. The treaty fixed Iran's eastern frontier under British influence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1857.jpg" alt="Treaty of Paris (1857)" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ILN Staff, after unidentified contributor to The Illustrated London News · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Farouk_Khan_1857_The_Illustrated_London_News.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
